  <p class="crumbs"><a href={project}>← Governed Agentic Empirical Research</a></p>
  <h1>What agentic-research does</h1>
  <p class="subtitle">Writing tooling for papers and proposals, installed once instead of copied</p>
  <p class="lede">
    agentic-research is a Claude Code plugin that sets up and polices a paper, proposal or position-paper
    repository. One command scaffolds the repo, a compiling LaTeX skeleton for the venue, build-on-save
    scripts, a citation store that checks references are real, and a set of writing agents. It replaced a
    habit of copying template repositories. The same six agents had ended up in 23 near-identical copies
    that differed only by a hardcoded path.
  </p>
  <p class="pin">Describes <a href={`${repo}/VERSION`}>v1.8.0</a> at commit <code>b34bfd5</code>, read on 9 November 2026.</p>

